{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "60eaf2eb-fae4-8bdd-8df6-69c294c0a550",
  "created_at": "2026-03-06T14:06:57-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Mei Goldberg",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:09-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:14-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, hello. This is Mei Goldberg. I am calling about a deck permit. I have a rental property and the deck, the boards are rotted. So I am replacing the boards."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:25-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Just the boards, or the framing underneath too? The posts, the joists?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:30-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just the boards, the top part. Okay, the joists I looked, they are fine. So the boards only. My question is, does that count as new construction? Because I am not building a new deck. It is the same deck."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:44-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And is it the same size, same footprint, nothing getting bigger or higher?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:50-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Same size. Same everything. Same footprint, yes, you said. Nothing bigger."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:04:55-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally, swapping out decking boards on an existing deck is treated as repair, not new construction. But I'd like the inspector's office to confirm, since it depends on what's underneath and how high off the ground it sits."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:08-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So maybe I do not need a permit. Maybe. Okay. I called last week to the other number and nobody picked up, so this is, you know, a hassle. Sorry. It is a simple thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:20-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's fair, and thanks for sticking with it. Is it a ground-level deck or up off the ground?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:27-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Up. Maybe four feet. Five? One flight of three steps, so, I think about four feet."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:33-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that matters a little. Go ahead with your other question."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:37-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. If I do need a permit, must a licensed contractor apply? Or can I, the owner, apply myself?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:44-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Owners can often apply for work on their own property, but with a rental there can be extra requirements. I'd rather have the inspector tell you exactly, so you don't hire someone you didn't need or skip something you did."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:05:58-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. That makes sense. Thank you. Oh, and one more, I am waiting for the rain to stop anyway, it is coming down today, so I will not start this weekend. Is that okay? I do not want to start before I know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:06:13-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a good idea. Hold off until you hear back. Let me take your number and have someone call you. Is it 401-555-0185?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:06:21-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, 401-555-0185, correct. You are on speaker, sorry, is it loud? I am in the car outside, taking photographs. I photograph old doorways around town, so I am walking and stopping."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:06:32-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I can hear you fine. I'll note it's a rental deck, boards only, about four feet high, same footprint, and the question about owner or contractor applying."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:06:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, yes, exactly. Boards only, four feet, same footprint, owner or contractor. Thank you so much. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:06:49-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Someone will call you back, likely early next week. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-06T14:06:55-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye-bye."
    }
  ],
